-- title:
--   An absorbing option-valued loop aborts at a reached step
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be any state type, and for each $k\in\mathbb N$ let $f_k$ be a charged computation from optional states to optional states. Write $\bot$ for an absent state and assume it is absorbing: $\operatorname{value}(f_k(\bot))=\bot$ for every $k$. Starting from a present state $b$, let $H_k$ be the value after the first $k$ bodies $f_0,\ldots,f_{k-1}$. For every $N\in\mathbb N$, $$H_N=\bot\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\exists k<N,\ c\in B:\ H_k=c\text{ is present and }\operatorname{value}(f_k(c))=\bot.$$ This identifies an abort in the actual execution prefix, rather than an arbitrary possible state.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ConditionalObservationAbortMass.lean#L39-L75

